  .hero__index-head { animation-delay: 560ms; }
  .hcell:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: 740ms; }
  .hcell:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 800ms; }
  .hcell:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 860ms; }
  .hcell:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 920ms; }
  /* The cue arrives LAST, and it was arriving FIRST. It shares the staged
     group above, and it was the only member with no delay: `animation-delay`
     defaulted to 0, so the invitation to leave the page started its 12px lift
     before the sentence the page exists to land had begun to ink in. Its
     parent's own opacity hid the result, which is why it was never caught by
     eye — but the two items on that baseline, the eyebrow and the cue, were
     lifting on different clocks for 160ms, and the order was wrong on the one
     axis motion is allowed to carry here. The order is now the reading order:
     clause 220 · claim 240 · ledger head 560 · rule 640 · names 740–920 ·
     the way out 1040. */
  .hero__scroll { animation-delay: 1040ms; }

