  /* THE TABLET BAND, 721–900. Figure swaps to focalSm/zoomSm at 720px, but
     the ledger goes to its one-row-per-pilot manifest at 900 — so between the
     two the frame is portrait, the ledger is 240px tall, and the crop is still
     the landscape one. The pair ends up behind the manifest. Custom properties
     inherit, and .fig resolves --zoom / --focal from --zoom-base / --focal-sm
     etc. on itself, so the override has to land on .fig directly.

     It takes the phone's focal-y (135%, inside the 137.7% foot cap derived at
     the top of this file — the cap is height-independent, so one number holds
     from a 667px phone to a 1200px tablet) but keeps its OWN horizontal. 31%
     is not 34% because the frame is not the same shape: the pair renders
     613px wide in a 768px frame and fits whole, so it is centred on 31.5%
     rather than pushed left to clear a 390px edge. Same photograph, three
     compositions, one per frame shape. */
  @media (min-width: 721px) and (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero :global(.hero__bg) { --zoom: 1.16; --focal: 31% 135%; }
  }

  /* Four names cannot hold one line each in four columns below this. The
